## Contributing

Commit messages follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org). The path a
commit touches decides which crate it bumps: `crates/csp-shell` moves the `csp-shell-v…` tag,
`crates/csp-policy` moves its own, and release-please rewrites the version requirement between
them so the pair cannot disagree about which release is being built.

Every gate a pull request has to pass is in [.github/workflows/ci.yml](.github/workflows/ci.yml),
and all of them run locally:

```bash
cargo fmt --all --check
cargo hack --workspace --feature-powerset clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings
cargo hack --workspace --each-feature test
cargo test --workspace --all-features
cargo build -p csp-shell --no-default-features --target thumbv7em-none-eabi
cargo deny check
```

Fuzzing lives in a workspace of its own under each crate's `fuzz/`. The oracles are an ordinary
library there, so the committed seeds and a deterministic sweep through them replay on a plain
`cargo test`, with no sanitizer and no nightly:

```bash
cd crates/csp-policy/fuzz && cargo test
cd crates/csp-shell/fuzz  && cargo test
```

A campaign discovers inputs rather than re-checking known ones, needs nightly, and is described in
[crates/csp-shell/README.md](crates/csp-shell/README.md).

